---
layout: layouts/page.njk
title: Style guide
eyebrow: Dev only, never published
lede: The building blocks of the site, in one place.
permalink: /styleguide/
---
<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>Palette</h2>
    <div class="sg-block sg-swatches">
      {%- for color in [
        { name: "Black", hex: "#0B0B0D" },
        { name: "Dark red", hex: "#8B0D0D" },
        { name: "Fire orange", hex: "#FF4A00" },
        { name: "Ivory", hex: "#E6D9C2" },
        { name: "Anthracite", hex: "#2A2A2E" },
        { name: "Antique gold", hex: "#D4A552" }
      ] %}
      <div class="sg-swatch">
        <div class="sg-swatch__chip" style="background: {{ color.hex }}"></div>
        <span>{{ color.name }}<br>{{ color.hex }}</span>
      </div>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>

    <h2>Typography</h2>
    <div class="sg-block">
      <h1 style="font-size: var(--step-6)">Independent worlds</h1>
      <h2 style="font-size: var(--step-5)">Unforgettable</h2>
      <h3 style="font-size: var(--step-4)">Experiences</h3>
      <h4 style="font-size: var(--step-3)">Cinzel for titles</h4>
      <p class="eyebrow">Montserrat for labels and interface</p>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Montserrat carries all running text. A studio site is read in small moments, so paragraphs stay short, the line length stays comfortable and ivory never reaches full brightness outside of titles.</p>
        <p><a href="#main">A text link</a> sits quietly until it is needed.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>Components</h2>
    <div class="sg-block">
      <div class="sg-row">
        <a class="btn btn--primary" href="#main">Primary action</a>
        <a class="btn" href="#main">Secondary action</a>
      </div>
      <div class="needle" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      {% placeholder "Any asset we do not have yet", "21 / 9" %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
